[DIMENSION POUCH SYSTEM - 차원 주머니]

## Concept
{{user}} carries a '차원 주머니' (Dimension Pouch) - a Sanctuary-issued spatial storage tied to the System. Every consumable item gained from gacha (Supply/Couple Item) and dungeon loot (gathered food, dropped supplies) is automatically stored inside it. cv_items reflects exactly what is in the pouch at any given moment.

## Rules (ABSOLUTE)
1. Universal Access: The pouch can be opened anywhere - Sanctuary, dungeon corridor, mid-combat lull, floor transitions. There is NO location restriction on retrieving items.
2. Time-Frozen Contents: Time does not flow inside the pouch. Food NEVER spoils, potions NEVER weaken, perishables stay perfect indefinitely. {{user}} can carry a hot meal for 100 days and pull it out steaming.
3. Instant Retrieval: Pulling an item out is instantaneous - a brief shimmer of light, the item appears in {{user}}'s hand. No fumbling, no searching. The pouch knows what {{user}} reaches for.
4. One Item, One Use (ABSOLUTE): Every general consumable in the pouch is SINGLE-USE. Use format `[SYSTEM|ITEM_USE: 이름]` (no quantity) - the item is permanently gone. The Lua backend enforces this by removing the inventory key entirely on ITEM_USE match. Always pair with the appropriate effect tag: [SYSTEM|HUNGER:+N 음식 섭취] / [SYSTEM|HP:+N 포션 사용] / etc.
 EXCEPTION - 가챠 티켓: 가챠 티켓 is the only stackable resource. Use the counter format `[SYSTEM|ITEM_USE: 가챠 티켓 x1]` - deducts 1 per use; do NOT delete the entire stack.

## In-Dungeon Usage (CRITICAL)
This system explicitly OVERRIDES the older "can only eat in safe zones" assumption. {{user}} can:
- Eat food mid-floor when hunger drops, even between monster encounters.
- Drink HP/MANA potions during exploration without retreating.
- Use utility items (trap detector, light source, etc.) on the spot.

Narration should treat retrieval as quick, natural, and slightly magical - companions might comment on the convenience or tease {{user}} for snacking in dangerous places, but the act itself takes only a beat. Do NOT block consumption with "you can only eat in the Sanctuary" or similar restrictions.

### EXCLUSIONS (still restricted by other rules)
- Mana Charging (companion-based intimate ritual) is STILL Sanctuary/Safe-Zone only - that is a relationship act, not an item, and is governed by the Mana System's Location & Limit rule.
- Item-based mana recovery (포션, 회복약) is allowed anywhere, including mid-dungeon, because it consumes a finite pouch item.

## Narrative Flavor Cues
- First mention per session: describe the pouch briefly ("손등에 살짝 스치자 차원 주머니가 푸르스름하게 빛나며…").
- Subsequent uses: keep it tight ("주머니에서 빵을 꺼냈다").
- Companions may occasionally comment: "역시 차원 주머니 덕에 굶을 일은 없네." / "던전에서 따뜻한 식사라니, 사치네요."
- Do NOT over-narrate the pouch every time - once established, treat it as ambient infrastructure.
- Couple Item mana recovery is the exception: because it is an intimate/rest-scene support item, it follows the Couple Gacha safe-zone rule (성소/성역/private safe rest space only).
